linear search:
public class Main{
    public static void main(String[] args){
        int[] ar={1,2,3,4,5};
        int target=4;
        for(int i=0;i<ar.length;i++){
            if(ar[i]==target){
                System.out.println(ar[i]);
                return;
            }
        }
        System.out.println("not found");
    }
}
algorithm:
1. Start from the first element.
2. Compare the current element with the target.
3. If they are equal → Target found.
4. If they are not equal → Move to the next element.
5. Repeat until the target is found or the array ends.
6. If the array ends → Target not found.

binary search:What is Binary Search?

Binary Search searches for an element by repeatedly checking the middle element and eliminating half of the remaining elements.

public class Main{
    public static void main(String[] args){
        int[] ar={1,2,3,4,5};
        int target=2;
        int low=0;
        int high=ar.length-1;
        while(low<=high){
            int mid=low+(high-low)/2;
            if(ar[mid]==target){
                System.out.println("found"+ar[mid]);
                return;
            }
            else if(target>ar[mid]){
               low=mid+1;
            }
            else{
                high=mid-1;
            }
        }
    }
}                                                      
    
              Binary Search
                    ↓
             Find middle
                    ↓
          ┌─────────┼─────────┐
          ↓         ↓         ↓
       Smaller     Equal    Greater
          ↓         ↓         ↓
        LEFT      FOUND     RIGHT
          ↓                   ↓
   high = mid - 1       low = mid + 1         

